---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="How It Works - MathSonify Mathematical Audio Architecture" description="Discover how MathSonify parses math equations, samples coordinates, and synthesizes audio in real-time.">
  <Navigation />

  <main class="min-h-screen pt-20 pb-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16 sc-reveal">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border border-sc-accent/40 bg-sc-accent/15 rounded-full font-mono text-xs text-sc-accent mb-4" data-i18n="howItWorks.tag">
        architectural specification
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-sc-text tracking-tight mb-4" data-i18n="howItWorks.title">
        How math becomes music
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.subtitle">
        MathSonify is not a random sound generator. It implements a deterministic mathematical translation engine that converts geometric properties of equations into acoustic properties of sound.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The pipeline -->
    <div class="space-y-8 sc-reveal-stagger">
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <div class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sc-accent/15 border border-sc-accent/50 text-sc-accent font-mono font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            01
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 flex-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-sc-text" data-i18n="howItWorks.step1Title">Safe AST equation parsing</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.step1Desc">
              When you enter a formula like <code class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-sc-sunken text-sc-accent font-mono text-xs border border-sc-line/15">sin(x) * cos(3*x)</code>, MathSonify uses <code class="text-sc-text">mathjs</code> to compile it into an abstract syntax tree (AST). We never execute raw <code class="text-red-400">eval()</code>, ensuring complete client-side security and eliminating code injection risks.
            </p>
            <div class="p-3 code-mat text-xs" data-i18n="howItWorks.step1Code">
              Input string, tokenizer, AST expression tree, compiled function
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <div class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sc-accent/15 border border-sc-accent/50 text-sc-accent font-mono font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            02
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 flex-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-sc-text" data-i18n="howItWorks.step2Title">High-resolution sampling and derivative estimation</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.step2Desc">
              The compiled equation is sampled across your chosen domain [x_min, x_max] at 600–800 discrete points. For each point we compute the coordinate (x, y), estimate the first derivative (slope dy/dx), and compute local curvature:
            </p>
            <div class="p-3 code-mat text-xs" data-i18n="howItWorks.step2Code">
              slope(x) = [f(x + dx) - f(x - dx)] / 2dx
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <div class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sc-accent/15 border border-sc-accent/50 text-sc-accent font-mono font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            03
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 flex-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-sc-text" data-i18n="howItWorks.step3Title">Acoustic parameter mapping</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.step3Desc">
              Mathematical dimensions are mapped to audio physics:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-sc-text-soft">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-sc-accent font-bold">•</span>
                <span data-i18n="howItWorks.step3x"><strong class="text-sc-text">Horizontal coordinate (x):</strong> mapped directly to the audio timeline and clock progress.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-sc-accent font-bold">•</span>
                <span data-i18n="howItWorks.step3y"><strong class="text-sc-text">Vertical elevation (y):</strong> normalized to audio pitch or quantized to musical scale degrees (e.g. minor pentatonic).</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-sc-accent font-bold">•</span>
                <span data-i18n="howItWorks.step3dy"><strong class="text-sc-text">Curve slope (|dy/dx|):</strong> dynamically opens the biquad lowpass filter cutoff to introduce higher harmonic brightness during steep transitions.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <div class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sc-accent/15 border border-sc-accent/50 text-sc-accent font-mono font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            04
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 flex-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-sc-text" data-i18n="howItWorks.step4Title">Real-time Web Audio API synthesis</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.step4Desc">
              We construct custom audio routing graphs inside the browser using native <code class="text-sc-text">AudioContext</code>:
            </p>
            <div class="p-3 code-mat text-xs space-y-1">
              <div>OscillatorNode (sine, triangle, saw, pulse) → BiquadFilterNode</div>
              <div>→ gain envelope (ADSR) → DynamicsCompressorNode → AnalyserNode → destination</div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-sc-text-soft" data-i18n="howItWorks.step4Note">
              A master <code class="text-sc-accent">DynamicsCompressorNode</code> ensures zero audio clipping, guarding your ears against sudden mathematical spikes or asymptotes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 5 -->
      <div class="panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start gap-6">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-sc-accent/15 border border-sc-accent/50 text-sc-accent font-mono font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            05
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 flex-1">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-sc-text" data-i18n="howItWorks.step5Title">Audio-visual synchronized playback</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-sc-text-soft leading-relaxed" data-i18n="howItWorks.step5Desc">
              As the audio context synthesizes the waveform, a 60 FPS animation loop drives the canvas 2D engine. The playhead traces the exact mathematical point on screen while the curve and spectrum state respond to the sound output.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-16 text-center sc-reveal">
      <a href="/create" class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center px-8 py-3.5 text-base" data-i18n="howItWorks.cta">
        Try it in the sound studio
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>